  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/ub0i1Roguh0VykvMYjTBnPZBFg5b20aVJPzytT7IND8.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nSome inferences from above data\n- $a q \\mathrm{~K}_2 \\mathrm{CO}_3$ can facilitate aldol condensation to aliphatic aldehydes.\n- HCN can lead to cyanohydrin formation\n- $\\mathrm{H}^{+}, \\Delta$ can lead to hydrolysis of cyanide to acid and following esterification. So $S$ is cyanohydrin.<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/PSYRzrrQMjFhPEo-HPgMnRsEh0hKBpYpzHThIfd51OA.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nCarbonyl compounds (Aldol condensation) Conceptual reaction and mechanistic understanding IV",
